.private/
# TASK-88: .private-remote is NOT ignored. It holds the sidecar's git URL and
# nothing else - the repo it names is private and access is controlled by SSH
# keys, so the URL is not a credential. Ignoring it made CLAUDE.md's bootstrap
# line `git clone "$(cat .private-remote)" .private` unrunnable in exactly the
# situation it exists for: a fresh clone, where the file it reads was never
# committed. That happened for real; the remote had to be recovered by listing
# GitHub repos and guessing.
